// A stdlib union signature is statically enforced (crypto C1/C2): `crypto.sha256` takes
// `string|bytes`, so an `int` argument is a type mismatch at the call site — SigType::Union
// maps onto the language's declared-union type and rides the ordinary assignability check.
// expect: error E0007 at 6:6
use std.{crypto}
echo crypto.sha256(42).to_hex()
